sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Athlete
  participant UI as CoachConnect page
  participant API as Vercel booking API
  participant Auth as Supabase Auth
  participant DB as PostgreSQL transaction
  participant RLS as RLS permission rules
  participant Coach as Coach dashboard

  Athlete->>UI: Choose an available future slot
  UI->>API: POST booking request + slot ID
  API->>Auth: Verify secure session
  alt Not signed in
    Auth-->>API: No valid member
    API-->>UI: 401 — sign in first
  else Signed in
    Auth-->>API: Authenticated member ID
    API->>RLS: Check athlete may book this coach
    alt Self-booking or unauthorized
      RLS-->>API: Denied
      API-->>UI: Clear permission message
    else Allowed
      RLS-->>API: Allowed
      API->>DB: Begin one atomic transaction
      Note right of DB: Atomic means all booking steps succeed together or none are saved.
      DB->>DB: Recheck future slot, coach status and availability
      DB->>DB: Insert booking under unique active-slot rule
      alt Another athlete already booked it
        DB-->>API: Conflict — transaction rolled back
        API-->>UI: Slot just became unavailable - choose another
      else Booking succeeds
        DB-->>API: Confirmed booking record
        API-->>UI: Show confirmation once
        API-->>Coach: Booking appears in coach dashboard
      end
    end
  end

  Note over Athlete,Coach: Cancellation records who cancelled and when.<br/>It frees the slot safely and displays policy wording.<br/>CoachConnect never holds money and cannot issue refunds.
